  "markdown": "# Materi 1 (Sesi 1-2): Introduction to E-Business Strategy and the Indonesian Business Landscape\n\n> [!info] Learning Outcome (syllabus)\n> LO1 (C6): evaluate the global strategic importance of e-business, including AI impact.\n> LO2 (C3): apply strategic analysis tools (SWOT, PESTEL) to formulate e-business strategies.\n> LO3 (C5): create user-centered e-business strategies (UX, A/B testing, interface design, AI personalization).\n> LO4 (C6): evaluate strategy impact with KPIs, ROI, and AI-driven analytics.\n\n> [!info] Cara baca\n> Ringkasan ini mengikuti urutan slide dosen. Tiap bagian = satu slide atau topik, dan **gambar slide ada tepat di bawah teks yang menjelaskannya**. Teks dikutip dari slide (bahasa asli), judul bagian dari judul slide.\n\n## Slide 3\n- TOPIC : Introduction to E-Business Strategy and the Indonesian Business Landscape\n- Definition and Evolution of E-Business\n- Importance of E-Business in Modern Business\n- Overview of the Indonesian Business Landscape\n- Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia\n- Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n\n## Definition and Evolution of E-Business\n- Definition\n- E-Business, short for electronic business, refers to the utilization of digital technologies and the internet to conduct various business processes, transactions, and interactions.\n- It involves the seamless integration of information and communication technologies (ICT) to streamline and optimize key aspects of business operations, including but not limited to, marketing, sales, supply chain management, and customer service.\n- E-business goes beyond the traditional brick-and-mortar model, embracing a virtual and interconnected approach that enables organizations to transcend geographical boundaries and interact with a global audience.\n- **In the e-business landscape:**\n- the internet serves as a fundamental platform for communication, collaboration, and commerce.\n- It (internet) facilitates not only the exchange of goods and services but also the exchange of information and knowledge among businesses, customers, and other stakeholders.\n- E-business encompasses a spectrum of digital activities, including e-commerce (online buying and selling), online marketing, electronic data interchange (EDI), digital payment systems, and the use of various online platforms for business transactions.\n\n## Definition and Evolution of E-Business\n- Evolution of e-business\n\n![Slide 5: Definition and Evolution of E-Business](bank/img/eb-1/slide05_1.png)\n\n## Importance of E-Business in Modern Business\n- Significance of E-Business\n\n## Importance of E-Business in Modern Business\n- BENEFITS\n\n## Overview of the Indonesian Business Landscape\n- MAPS\n- Produksi/Cadangan (C) Indonesia\n- Produksi/Cadangan (C) Global\n- Pangsa Total Indonesia\n- Cocoa\n- 420,000 ton\n- 4,025,000 ton\n- 10.4%\n- Coalbed Methane﻿﻿\n- 453 triliun kaki kubik (C)\n- 7,550 triliun kaki kubik (C)\n- 6.0%\n- Batubara\n- 241.1 mln tons oil equiv.\n- 3,830.1 mln tons oil equiv.\n- 6.3%\n- Beras\n- 70.6 juta ton\n- 744.0 juta ton\n- 9.5%\n- Emas\n- 109.9 ton\n- 3,109.0 ton\n- 3.5%\n- Energi Panas Bumi\n- 27,510 MW (R)\n- 68,775 MW (R)\n- 40.0%\n- Gas Alam\n- 75.0 billion m³\n- 3538.6 billion m³﻿\n- 2.1%\n- Karet (Alam)\n- 3.2 million tons*\n- 12 million tons*\n- 26.7%\n- Kopi\n- 9.4 million 60 kg bags\n- 141.7 million 60 kg bags\n- 6.6%\n- Minyak Bumi\n- 825,000 bpd\n- 91,670,000 bpd\n- 0.9%\n- Minyak Kelapa Sawit\n- 31.0 juta ton\n- 60.0 juta ton\n- 51.7%\n- Teh\n- 0.13 juta ton\n- 5.03 juta ton\n- 2.6%\n\n![Slide 8: Overview of the Indonesian Business Landscape](bank/img/eb-1/slide08_1.png)\n\n## Overview of the Indonesian Business Landscape\n- key points of interest when examining the business landscape:\n\n## Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia\n- Positioning Indonesia Globally\n\n![Slide 10: Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia](bank/img/eb-1/slide10_1.png)\n\n![Slide 10: Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia](bank/img/eb-1/slide10_2.png)\n\n## Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia\n- Positioning Indonesia Globally\n\n![Slide 11: Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia](bank/img/eb-1/slide11_1.png)\n\n![Slide 11: Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia](bank/img/eb-1/slide11_2.png)\n\n## Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia\n- Positioning Indonesia Globally\n\n![Slide 12: Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia](bank/img/eb-1/slide12_1.png)\n\n![Slide 12: Key Economic Sectors in Indonesia](bank/img/eb-1/slide12_2.png)\n\n## Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n- Trends and challenges\n\n## Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n- Digital Adoption\n- **Exploring Digital Adoption:**\n- Indonesia is currently experiencing an unprecedented surge in digital adoption.\n- Individuals, businesses, and communities are actively embracing digital technologies, marking a transformative era.\n- **Increased Reliance on Digital Technologies:**\n- The nation's reliance on digital tools has expanded across various facets of life.\n- From personal communication to educational pursuits and commercial activities, digital adoption has become integral.\n\n![Slide 14: Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market](bank/img/eb-1/slide14_1.png)\n\n## Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n- E-Commerce BOOm\n\n![Slide 15: Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market](bank/img/eb-1/slide15_1.png)\n\n## Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n- Mobile connectivity\n- Undang-undang Nomor 11 Tahun 2020 Tentang Cipta Kerja (Lembaran Negara Republik Indonesia Tahun 2020 Nomor 245, Tambahan Lembaran Negara Republik Indonesia Nomor 6573)\n\n![Slide 16: Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market](bank/img/eb-1/slide16_1.png)\n\n![Slide 16: Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market](bank/img/eb-1/slide16_2.png)\n\n## Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n- Infrastructure limitation\n\n## Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n- Regulatory complexity\n\n## Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market\n- Consumer Behaviour shifts\n- **Mobile-First Consumption:**\n- **Social Commerce Influence:**\n- **Rise of Online Marketplaces:**\n- **Preference for Cash-on-Delivery (COD):**\n- **Localized Content and Language:**\n- **Rapid Adoption of Digital Wallets:**\n- **Increased Focus on Customer Experience:**\n- **Sustainability and Social Responsibility:**\n- **Loyalty Programs and Discounts:**\n- **Cross-Border Shopping:**\n- **Virtual Events and Livestream Shopping:**\n- **Concerns about Security and Privacy:**\n- https://www.retaileconomics.co.uk/plugins/ckeditor/plugins/imageuploader/uploads/27674a78d.JPG\n\n![Slide 19: Current Trends and Challenges in the Indonesian Market](bank/img/eb-1/slide19_1.png)\n\n## Slide 20\n- TOPIC : Introduction to E-Business Strategy and the Indonesian Business Landscape\n- REFERENCES\n- Chaffey, D., Edmundson-Bird, D., & Hemphill, T. (2019). Digital business and e-commerce management. Pearson UK.\n- Laudon, K. C., & Traver, C. G. (2020). E-commerce: Business, Technology, Society. Pearson.\n"
